course: dictionary
lesson: 7728
title: Pufferfish: blowing up to stay safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pufferfish is a fish that can blow itself up into a big, round ball. It does this by gulping water very quickly. «A pufferfish gulps water into a stretchy stomach and swells to several times its size.» Swells means grows much bigger, and the water is what makes it bigger.
explain: Why does it do this? A pufferfish blows up to scare off predators, which are animals that hunt other animals. A big, round, often spiky ball is hard to swallow, so a hungry predator may swim away. Context helps here: the words «hard to swallow» and «scare off» tell you the puffing is a way to stay safe.
explain: Puffing up is tiring and stressful, so the pufferfish only does it when it must. «It does not do it for fun.» That sentence is a clue that the pufferfish saves this trick for danger. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «stressful» means «making you feel worried», does the sentence still make sense? It does.
explain: Many pufferfish are also poisonous. «Pufferfish swallow water fast to blow up into a prickly ball, and many also have strong poison.» Many means not all, so always be careful with any pufferfish you see.
fact: A pufferfish is also called a puffer or a blowfish.
fact: «Venomous» means an animal pushes venom into you with a bite or sting, but «poisonous» means harmful if you touch or eat it. A pufferfish is poisonous, not venomous.
fact: In Japan, pufferfish is called «fugu», and only chefs with a special licence may prepare it.
fact: Some male pufferfish make beautiful circle patterns in the sand to attract females.
fact: «Pufferfish» is a noun, and its plural is also pufferfish: one pufferfish, two pufferfish.
exercise: A pufferfish blows itself up to scare off predators. What is a predator? | *An animal that hunts other animals for food | A rock that rolls down a hill | A fish that lives in a pond | A plant that grows in the sea
exercise: «Venomous and poisonous are not the same.» Which animal is poisonous, not venomous? | A scorpion | *A pufferfish | A snake
exercise: «Pufferfish, called fugu in Japan, have a very strong poison.» What does fugu mean? | *Pufferfish in Japan | A kind of Japanese soup | A stretchy stomach | A deep sea diver
test: Why does a pufferfish swallow water? | *To blow itself up to scare off predators | To make its colours brighter | Because it is thirsty and wants a drink | To sink to the bottom and rest
test: Why does the pufferfish only puff up when it must? | *Because puffing up is tiring and stressful | Because it is shy of the other fish | Because it is bored of being round
exam: Which word means harmful if you touch or eat it? | Stretchy | Venomous | Prickly | *Poisonous
